v064lnev@ubvmsb.cc.buffalo.edu (Zerxes Bhagalia) writes:

>	I am currently supporting NetHack 3.0.10 on my system.  I would like to
>know how I can disable the SHELL command.  I would greatly appreciate it if

You didn't say what kind of operating system you'd like to disable the shell
on. Anyway, one solution on any system would be to just compile the game
yourself without the shell command option.

If you can't do that, one thing you could do, if you run MS-DOS, would be
to put 
	SET COMSPEC= <some harmless program that does nothing>
in the .BAT file you use to start the game, just before the nethack command.
Then, after the nethack command you just set comspec back to what it usually
is. And this thing works, I've tried it with a program that just displays
the time and date on the screen.

I don't know how this would be done on unix.
